          "heading": "England men's rugby hopes boosted by new Prem refereeing law interpretations",
          "body": "Steve Borthwick has secured a tactical shift for the upcoming season, with Prem Rugby agreeing to new refereeing interpretations designed to align domestic club matches more closely with the international game. Targeted areas include the scrum’s brake-foot law and the offside line, as well as greater officiating consistency at the breakdown. Borthwick, aiming to challenge South Africa’s international dominance, hopes these changes will better prepare his squad for the intensity and breakdown contests expected at next year's World Cup."
