          "heading": "Wales Women Lose Scrum-Half Seren Lockwood For USA Test After HIA",
          "body": "Scrum-half Seren Lockwood has been ruled out of Wales Women's second WXV Global Series fixture against the USA after failing a head injury assessment. Lockwood was forced off during the first half of the eight-try victory over South Africa and is currently following World Rugby's return to play protocols. Her absence paves the way for Lleucu George to return at 10, with Keira Bevan reverting to her usual position of nine at Cardiff Arms Park. Head coach Sean Lynn noted that whilst it is sad to see an individual come off, the HIA process is important for player welfare."
